    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9176-2",
        "name": "USN-9176-2",
        "description": "USN-9176-1 fixed vulnerabilities in Ruby. This update provides the corresponding updates for Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled converting the case  of certain strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a  denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-34m4-m9fh-gqp5)   Owais Lone discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled compiling certain  large regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to  cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-3p8q-wmhx-vm2w)   Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled converting certain  regular expressions to strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue  to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-7whj-  cfh7-xgm4)   Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled memory when parsing  certain regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to  cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-7x2q-68qv-6p8x)   It was discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled converting the case of  certain large strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause  a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-87fm-7w84-j2px)   It was discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled certain case-insensitive  regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a  denial of service or obtain sensitive information. (GHSA-pvgc-g7gj-pv6h)   Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled certain case-  insensitive regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue  to cause a denial of service or obtain sensitive information. (GHSA-  wpqw-5qxg-m68r)",
        "aliases": []
      },
